Fixed and committed (3b240bdd): plain yoyo -p and piped input without --print no longer start stdout with blank lines. Fmt, clippy (-D warnings) and the full test suite pass.

Reproduction: I ran the exact recorded command (from /tmp, no config, no flags added, default model claude-opus-4-6) and got \n\n\nPONG\n\n. --output-format stream-json shows the model's first text chunk is "\n\nPONG". So two of the leading newlines come from the model, and the third is a newline yoyo itself writes when the first text arrives (write_stream_text("\n") in src/prompt.rs). Both go through the same stdout write path, so one filter there removes all three.

Fix:
• **New src/stream_leading_blank.rs** holds the single version of the rule, `strip_leading_blank_lines`. I moved it out of `main.rs`, and `answer_payload` (the Day-212 fix for `--print` and json) now calls it, so the two doors can't drift apart.
• **`LeadingBlankFilter`** holds back only leading whitespace. Real text goes out with the same chunk that carries it, and indentation on the first content line is kept.
• **Wiring:** `write_stream_text` and the stdout branch of `write_chrome` both pass through the filter. `main.rs` switches it on only for unreserved `-p` and piped input. The interactive REPL never switches it on, so its output is unchanged.
• **Piped input** got the fix too, though the task only named `-p`. It had the same bug and goes through the same code path, and I didn't want to fix one of the two scripting doors and leave the other.

Measured after: both -p and piped now print PONG\n\n. Trailing newlines are still written, as before.

Tests:
• Five unit tests cover the cases the task listed, including the whitespace-only stream, which writes nothing. Two more check that real text is released immediately and that output is unchanged when the filter is off (the REPL case).
• A process-level test, plain_prompt_mode_still_streams_model_leading_blank_lines, used to assert that the old blank lines reached stdout unchanged. I rewrote it to assert the new contract (stdout is exactly ANSWER\n\n) and noted in its doc comment what it used to pin. It still has the old name, which now reads wrong.
• **Positive control:** I disabled the filter (with a `NEUTERED` marker), and the three filter tests plus the process test failed by name while both near-miss tests stayed green. After I restored it, all tests passed and no marker was left.

Other changes:
• `CHANGELOG.md` has an Unreleased line.
• `docs/src/usage/single-prompt.md said -p` might print leading blank lines on purpose, which is no longer true, so I corrected it.
• `src/prompt.rs grew by 2 lines, so I updated its entry in the module-size register in tests/module_size.rs` (3790 → 3792) and added a comment saying why.

Not done: I didn't add a history entry to ARCHITECTURE.md for this change.
